#: src/i18n/interpolation.md:76
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// Reference the base key without any suffix — Perry picks the plural "
"variant\n"
"// from the `count` parameter and the current locale's CLDR rules.\n"
"const cartCount = 3\n"
"const itemMessage = t(\"You have {count} items\", { count: cartCount })\n"
"console.log(itemMessage)\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/i18n/interpolation.md:84
msgid ""
"Perry detects the plural parameter from the first `{param}` placeholder in "
"the key (here `{count}`). At runtime, each call site evaluates the current "
"locale's CLDR rules against the passed value and selects the matching form's "
"translation — a compiled binary run with `LANG=de_DE.UTF-8` picks the German "
"`.one` form for `count: 1` and the German `.other` form for `count: 3`. A "
"call site that doesn't pass the plural parameter renders the base "
"(non-plural) key."
msgstr ""

