#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:1
msgid "Node builtin-module Compatibility Matrix"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:3
msgid ""
"Perry reimplements the `node:*` module surface natively. The **compatibility "
"matrix** (`scripts/node_compat_matrix.mjs`) measures — against a _pinned, "
"verified_ Node — how faithfully Perry reproduces each builtin's **export "
"shape**, for **both** import forms (`M` and `node:M`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:8
msgid ""
"Its value is **breadth**: every builtin, both forms, one pinned oracle. It "
"is the systematic version of tracker "
"[\\#812](https://github.com/PerryTS/perry/issues/812) (\"42-module "
"behavioral matrix\"). Deep _behavioral_ parity lives in the hand-authored "
"node-suite (`run_parity_tests.sh`); this harness is a wide, shallow "
"**shape** sweep."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:14
msgid "To check one module fast"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:20
msgid ""
"That is the command to reach for while iterating on a single builtin. The "
"pinned Node download happens once and is cached under `.cache/node-pin/`, so "
"subsequent runs are just Perry compile + run. Narrow further:"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:25
msgid "# a few modules"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:26
msgid "# only these exports"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:27
msgid "# combined mod.export form"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:30
msgid ""
"A `--method`/`--only` subset narrows the fingerprint to those exports for a "
"sub-second \"did my change fix `node:fs.readFileSync`?\" loop. Because it "
"changes the fingerprint semantics, it is a **print-only diagnostic** — it is "
"refused for `--check`/`--update-baseline`."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:35
msgid "Full sweep and the CI gate"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:38
msgid "# whole matrix + summary table"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:39
msgid "# exit 1 on regressions vs the baseline"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:40
msgid "# rewrite the committed baseline"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:43
msgid ""
"The harness needs the release binary (`cargo build --release -p perry`). The "
"baseline lives at `test-parity/node-compat-matrix.baseline.json`; the CI job "
"`.github/workflows/node-compat-matrix.yml` runs `--check` nightly in its own "
"job (so the pinned-Node download never slows the main test job)."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:48
msgid ""
"A baseline is **scoped to the platform and Node line it was generated "
"against** — platform-dependent surfaces (`os`, `path/win32`, `dgram`, `fs`, "
"`inspector`) and version-dependent export shapes only compare meaningfully "
"within that scope. `--check` therefore **refuses** to run when the "
"baseline's `platform`/`nodeVersion` header does not match the current run (a "
"cross-platform comparison would surface phantom regressions or mask real "
"ones), and refuses a vacuously green pass when a full sweep processed fewer "
"modules than the baseline records. The committed baseline is `darwin-arm64`, "
"so the nightly gate runs on a `macos-14` (Apple Silicon) runner to match it; "
"move the baseline to another platform by regenerating it there and pointing "
"the job at a matching runner."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:60
msgid ""
"`--check` fails when a baselined cell got **strictly worse** (per a severity "
"order: `match` → `shape-diff` → `perry-unresolved`) or when a "
"**prefix-parity** invariant that previously held broke. Improvements are "
"always accepted and are folded in by `--update-baseline`. A `--module` "
"selector scopes `--check`/`--update-baseline` to just that slice — a "
"single-module refresh never rewrites the whole baseline."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:67
msgid "The pin"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:69
msgid ""
"The oracle is the **official nodejs.org dist tarball** for the host "
"platform, a _binary_ pin (not a source checkout — we measure shape against "
"the runtime Node actually ships). It is recorded in `external-tools.json` "
"under `tools.node` with a `sha512` SRI per platform, matching that file's "
"existing convention. The runner downloads it, verifies the SRI, and caches "
"it under `.cache/node-pin/` (gitignored). nodejs.org also publishes "
"`SHASUMS256.txt` (sha256), which is cross-checked against every pinned asset "
"at pin time."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:77
msgid ""
"Currently pinned: **Node 26.5.1** (the latest CURRENT stable). This is a "
"separate concern from `.node-version` (26.5.0), which pins the gap-suite / "
"node-suite oracle; the compat matrix carries its own \"latest stable\" pin."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:81
msgid "The fingerprint"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:83
msgid "For a module `M` and a form, the probe does:"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:85
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import * as ns from \"M\"          // or \"node:M\"\n"
"// sorted list of `<exportName>:<typeof export[name]>` over "
"Object.keys(ns),\n"
"// plus `default:<typeof ns.default>`, wrapped in a __FP__...__FP__ "
"sentinel.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:91
msgid ""
"Two fingerprints are **equal** iff the two module namespaces have the same "
"export names with the same `typeof` for each, and the same default-export "
"`typeof`. It is a **shape** fingerprint (names + typeofs), not deep "
"behavior. The sentinel line means environmental warnings on stdout/stderr "
"never touch the compare — no output-normalization needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:97
msgid "Each `(module, form)` cell gets a status:"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:99
msgid "status"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:99
msgid "meaning"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:101
msgid "`match`"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:101
msgid "Perry fingerprint == oracle fingerprint"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:102
msgid "`shape-diff`"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:102
msgid "both resolved, fingerprints differ (a real shape gap)"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:103
msgid "`perry-unresolved`"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:103
msgid "Node resolved, Perry did not compile/run"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:104
msgid "`perry-extra`"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:104
msgid "Perry resolved a form the oracle did not"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:105
msgid "`both-unresolved`"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:105
msgid "neither resolved (neutral)"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:106
msgid "`skip`"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:106
msgid "curated skip — see `test-parity/node-compat-matrix.skip.json`"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:108
msgid ""
"Modules that cannot be meaningfully fingerprinted by a bare `import * as m` "
"(side-effectful on import, or shape depends on constructor args) go in the "
"skip JSON **with a reason** rather than silently passing."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:112
msgid "The prefixed / unprefixed invariant"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:114
msgid ""
"For builtins where Node resolves both `M` and `node:M`, Node treats the "
"forms identically and Perry's `is_native_module` strips the `node:` prefix — "
"so those two forms **must** agree. The runner records `prefixParity` for "
"that scope, and a `false` value is a **real Perry bug** that fails `--check` "
"if parity previously held."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:120
msgid ""
"Node also exposes prefix-only builtins such as `node:test`. The matrix still "
"probes their bare spelling, but records `prefixParity: null` because Node "
"has no two-form invariant there. If Perry accepts the bare alias, that cell "
"is reported as `perry-extra`: a documented leniency, not prefix parity."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:125
msgid "Bumping the pinned Node"
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:127
msgid ""
"Edit `tools.node.version` in `external-tools.json` and refresh the "
"per-platform `sha512` SRI (download each dist tarball, verify its sha256 "
"against that version's `SHASUMS256.txt`, then record the recomputed sha512)."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:130
msgid "`node scripts/node_compat_matrix.mjs --update-baseline`."
msgstr ""

#: src/testing/node-compat-matrix.md:131
msgid ""
"**Review the diff.** A Node bump legitimately changes fingerprints (new "
"exports, typeof changes); confirm the deltas are Node's, not Perry "
"regressions, before committing."
msgstr ""

